>   // ---- VARIANT A: static per-source partition of the landing zone ----
>   //
>   // Stock reserves from a single index_t allocator in the PEER's memory, so every
>   // block of every rank does a SYSTEM-scope RMW on one remote word: blockNum x
>   // npes x worldSize RMWs onto worldSize words. Measured on gfx1250 at EP4 /
>   // hidden 7168 / topk 6 / 512 tok-rank that is 10.87us mean (p95 21.6), the
>   // largest single item in the kernel -- of which only ~3.1us is the fabric round
>   // trip and 0.72us the barrier; the rest is queueing.
>   //
>   // The landing zone is ALREADY sized at EpMaxRecv == worldSize * maxTokPerRank,
>   // one full quota per source. So give source s the slot range
>   // [s*kSegStride, (s+1)*kSegStride) in every peer and the base becomes local: no
>   // peer has to arbitrate, because no two sources can name the same slot. Dedup
>   // caps a source at one slot per token per destination, so maxTokPerRank per
>   // (src,dst) is exactly sufficient.
>   //
>   // The only atomic left is the AGENT-scope one on destPeTokenCounter that the
>   // stock path already performs; its pre-increment return IS the offset inside
>   // our segment, so the remote RMW is removed at no added cost.
>   //
>   // COST: the landing zone is no longer one packed run. Consumers must either walk
>   // the four segments (counts are exported below) or compact -- see the README.
>   constexpr index_t kSegStride = (index_t)(EpMaxRecv(kCfg) / npes);
